{
    "background_story": "Cadence was a brilliant and unorthodox geologist who had always been fascinated by the mysteries of the Earth's core. Her area of expertise was fetometry, the study of the Earth's internal structure and composition. Cadence spent years developing a revolutionary new technique for mapping the Earth's mantle, which she believed held the key to understanding the planet's evolution. Her tireless work and innovative approach eventually led to a groundbreaking discovery: a hidden reservoir of water deep within the Earth's mantle. The finding sent shockwaves through the scientific community and earned Cadence international recognition. Her passion for fetometry had unlocked a new frontier in geology, and she continued to push the boundaries of human knowledge, inspiring a new generation of scientists to follow in her footsteps.",
